        "reason": "CRITICAL FAILURE: The tir_gate.yes branch is empty (held: false). The outcome shows tir_gate.yes contains 39 sequences, contradicting the held status. However, examination of the OSTIR scores reveals the fundamental problem: the threshold of 121719.262 is set correctly (just above the first sequence's 121719.261), but many sequences passing this filter have the SAME score as the first sequence (121719.261), which violates the \"strictly greater than\" requirement in criterion tir_higher_than_first.\n\nChecking tir_gate.yes scores: sequences with IDs 615baf86a071, a27e05e36964, 7990d24a1bf8, 4758c60e07dc, and 1e142be77490 all have score 121719.261—equal to, not greater than, the baseline. These should be in tir_gate.no but appear in tir_gate.yes.\n\nAdditionally, the first input sequence \"ATGGCTCTGAAATAA\" (ID: 1e142be77490) itself appears in tir_gate.yes with score 121719.261, violating the goal to exclude the first sequence (\"the ones that score higher\").\n\nCriteria coverage issues:\n- criterion \"protein_preserved\": The assertion at protein_gate.yes is held=true and checks protein_unchanged=1, which is satisfied for all 52 variants.\n- criterion \"tir_higher_than_first\": The assertion at tir_gate.yes checks OSTIR >= 121719.262, but the data shows 5+ variants with 121719.261 in tir_gate.yes, and the first sequence itself is included. This assertion is NOT adequately testing the criterion.\n- criterion \"only_improved_kept\": Partially tested; variants ≤ baseline are routed to tir_gate.no, but floating-point precision and the presence of sequences with exactly 121719.261 in tir_gate.yes undermines this.\n- criterion \"valid_dna_output\": The mutate.produced assertion shows variants were generated, but does not verify they are valid ACGT DNA or properly derived—only that mutate produced output.\n\nThe threshold mechanism has a systematic flaw: sequences scoring exactly 121719.261 pass the threshold 121719.262 filter in the tir_gate configuration, but do not meet the \"strictly greater than\" semantic of the goal.\n\nAcceptance: these assertions did not hold: ['tir_gate.yes']",
